<h1>Money Watch — Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="muted">Last updated: October 26, 2026</p>

<h2>Who we are</h2>
<p>Money Watch (Android app <code>com.usefulappz.moneywatch</code>) is developed by Usefulappz™ (Mike Kelley). Contact: <a href="mailto:mikekelleyii.mk2@gmail.com">mikekelleyii.mk2@gmail.com</a></p>

<h2>The short version</h2>
<p>Money Watch displays the watch state for the developer's own business revenue — whether new money has landed, and the running totals. It does <strong>not</strong> connect to your bank, holds no credentials, and moves no money. It collects <strong>no personal data from you</strong>: no accounts, no analytics, no ads SDK, no tracking, and nothing is sold.</p>

<h2>How the app works</h2>
<ul>
  <li>The watch itself runs on <strong>our server</strong>, over the developer's own sales and ledger records. The app fetches the current watch state — recent landings and totals — from our server and displays it. That fetch carries none of your information.</li>
  <li>If the live state cannot be reached, the app may show a clearly labeled snapshot from its last successful read. It never presents a snapshot as live data.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What the app stores</h2>
<p>Nothing about you. The app keeps no account, no profile, and no financial information of yours — it has no access to your bank, cards, or payment accounts, and it cannot send, receive, or move money.</p>

<h2>Permissions, and why</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Internet</strong> — used only to fetch the current watch state from our server, as described above.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Ads</h2>
<p>Money Watch contains <strong>no ads and no advertising SDK</strong>.</p>

<h2>Children</h2>
<p>Money Watch is a business tool. It is not directed at children under 13, and it collects no data from anyone.</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>If this policy changes, the new version will be posted at this URL with a new "last updated" date.</p>

